% ============================================================================
% shape-composition.query.adj — a worked recall over the DERIVED
% shape-composition fact.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how many triangles make
% up a square?": it states no geometry reasoning of its own — it only
% `import`s the library and asks a binding query. The engine derives the
% answer via the `rule` (composing the quadrilateral-types table with the
% triangulation/diagonal definitions) and returns it WITH the full two-step
% audit trail: the rule's own citation and the underlying quadrilateral
% fact's citation. The third query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% count `2`, recall every quadrilateral it holds for). A shape not in the
% quadrilateral-types table (a triangle, which has no diagonals to draw in
% the first place) abstains honestly — the engine never invents a count.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli shape-composition.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "shape-composition.adj"

? triangle_decomposition_count(square, $N)       % expect 2
? triangle_decomposition_count(trapezoid, $N)    % expect 2
? triangle_decomposition_count($Shape, 2)        % reverse bind — expect all 5 quadrilaterals
? triangle_decomposition_count(triangle, $N)     % expect abstain — a triangle has no diagonal to draw
